{"body":"## Summary\n\nFirst milestone of the 24-hour TOE campaign (`.claude/science/physics-loops/toe-campaign-20261015/`). The topic is **what one unitary tick can do on the axioms' lattice**, plus one formation-lane result.\n\n- Everything is bounded support and unaudited.\n- No axiom, primitive or dynamics clause is adopted.\n- Each claim is labelled as exact, numerical or open in its note.\n- The base is the hygiene branch (#9625), so this diff shows only campaign work.\n\n| Note | Runner | Main result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `CUBIC_COVARIANCE_FREEZES_A_ONE_QUBIT_TICK_…` | `cubic_covariant_qubit_walk_cell_classification_2026_10_16.py` (PASS=31) + `cubic_covariant_qubit_walk_line_branch_certificates_2026_10_16.py` (PASS=16) | **One qubit per site cannot move in a cubic-covariant tick.** A unitary walk on the 27-point cell that is covariant under translations and proper cubic rotations is a constant, under each of the four soldering-menu coin actions. With the full action the freeze persists at ranges two and three per axis (125- and 343-point stencils; range three uses a Singular-certified final step), which also rules out O-covariant split-step products of two cell steps. Also: T (order 12) freezes; D4 allows axial shifts only; D3 allows body-diagonal shifts only. So 3-D motion needs symmetry of order ≤ 4 (C3, C4, D2), which is exact for every larger subgroup, and the D2 product walk then carries a linear, handed dispersion term −n₁n₂n₃\\|k\\|². | Exact for O, T, D4 and all menu actions (Gröbner); independent Singular re-derivation agrees. Range two under O and D3 on the cell are exact by line-branch certificates. Fresh-context independent checks, each using a different method, confirm range two, D3 and the √(2/3) bound. The earlier numerical \"D3: none\" was wrong and has been corrected. |\n| `ORDER_BLIND_POSITIVE_FORMATION_IS_A_ONE_DEPENDENT_GIBBS_FIELD_…` | `order_blind_formation_one_dependent_record_field_2026_10_16.py` (PASS=17) | Strictly positive order-blind formation yields a single consistent infinite-volume record field. Its full conditionals equal the rule (the static and formation readings coincide). It is 1-dependent, so there is no long-range order, no power-law correlation and no pinch point, i.e. no Coulomb phase from this class. | General proofs; exact checks on the 48-point chiral-pair rule. |\n| `TWO_QUBIT_SITE_UNFREEZES_THE_CUBIC_TICK_DOUBLER_FREE_DIRAC_WALK_…` | `two_qubit_cubic_dirac_tick_2026_10_16.py` (PASS=40) | **A two-qubit site (the parked M₄(ℂ) fork) unfreezes the tick, and the walks it allows have Dirac structure.** Details below the table. | Exact: Clifford relations, Gram criterion, b\\*, speed bound, golden member, chirality freeze, staggering within the Clifford class. Numerical: spectrum, universality (7 samples), irreducible-coin and staggered searches. Independent check agrees and corrected one statement. |\n| `STAGGERED_ONE_QUBIT_BLOCKS_CARRY_A_CUBIC_COVARIANT_DIRAC_TICK_…` | `staggered_one_qubit_block_cubic_dirac_tick_2026_10_16.py` (PASS=11) | **The electron can be a neighbourhood.** One amplitude per site on staggered 2×2×2 blocks, with rotations acting about block centres. The spinorial signed corner action is two copies of spin 3/2, and it carries an exactly covariant moving Dirac tick: two Dirac fermions per block, like the KS taste pair. | Exact construction; spectrum numerical. A nearest-site version is open: the solutions found so far have flat bands. |\n\nDetails of the two-qubit result:\n- The walk family is U = f + i h·τ⊥ + i τ₃ ⊗ g·σ. Existence is classified by one Gram criterion: G(b) ⪰ 0 with rank ≤ 3.\n- An algebraic member has exactly one massless, isotropic Dirac cone, and all doublers are gapped.\n- The cone speed obeys s ≤ 1, and the axis doublers sit at quasienergy 2 arcsin s. So the walk is doubler-free iff s < 1.\n- The light-speed walk is unique and lies over ℚ(√5). Its dispersion is ω² = \\|k\\|² − (7/6 − √5/2)(\\|k\\|⁴ − Σkₐ⁴).\n- An exactly chiral walk is frozen, so the Wilson-type chirality breaking is forced. W₃ = 0 across the family.\n- The chirality-breaking k² term of the massless walk has exact size ½ sin θ_X (θ_X = axis-doubler quasienergy), a quantitative Nielsen–Ninomiya trade-off.\n- Parity staggering with covariance about every site does not unfreeze the tick; block-centred staggering does (new note above).\n- **Every irreducible coin freezes (exact):** E, spin ½, spin 1 and spin 3/2, so moving needs a reducible site or a neighbourhood.\n- **Isotropy budget (exact):** the massless band is cos ω = φ₀ᵀG(b)φ(k). The k⁴ cubic anisotropy is −s(b₀−b₁−2b₂)/3 · Σkₐ⁴, so it can be cancelled on a plane. There ω² = s²\\|k\\|² − s²(1−s²)\\|k\\|⁴/12 + …, and an unavoidable k⁶ anisotropy −(s²/360)\\|k\\|²Σkₐ⁴ remains. On that plane \\|s\\| ≤ √(2/3), attained at an explicit doubler-free member over ℚ(√6, √15). So light speed and k⁴ isotropy exclude each other.\n\n### What to check in review\n- **The reduction to f + i g·σ** (Theorem 0 in the freeze note) and its fixed-vector condition. All negative claims are made only for groups without a fixed vector.\n- **The Gram-uniqueness step** and the rank-3 certificate at b\\*.\n- **The line lemma** (B1 Theorems 4–5): on a line whose stabiliser fixes only that line, f + i\\|g\\| is a unit Laurent monomial.\n- **The √(2/3) argument** (B3 Theorem 7): compactness of the PSD part of the curve plus the discriminant.\n- **The scope of \"staggering is frozen\"**: it is exact within the Clifford class and otherwise rests on universality evidence.\n- **The relation to prior work:** D'Ariano–Perinotti BCC Weyl and Dirac automata, Bialynicki-Birula, Wilson-type quantum walks (arXiv:1807.08303), and doubling in 3+1-D Dirac walks (arXiv:2601.15885).\n\n### Open obligations (also listed in the handoff)\n- One-qubit freeze at every finite range (exact at ranges one to three).\n- Universality of the Clifford form for all two-qubit covariant walks.\n\n### Validation\n- All five runners pass: 31/31, 16/16, 17/17, 40/40, 11/11.\n- `repo_invariants_check.py --check --enforce-links`: PASS. The citation-graph manifest is refreshed for the three new notes.\n- Independent checks, run as fresh-context agents (same model family, new implementations, no access to the notes), have their scripts kept in the loop pack.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0186zYf1gqhH6RqwTgVb8jro\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_","files":[{"path":".claude/commands/autopilot.md","additions":2,"deletions":2},{"path":".claude/commands/physics-loop.md","additions":27,"deletions":126},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/toe-campaign-20261015/HANDOFF.md","additions":66,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/toe-campaign-20261015/OPPORTUNITY_QUEUE.md","additions":21,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/toe-campaign-20261015/STATE.yaml","additions":66,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/toe-campaign-20261015/exact_extensions/README.md","additions":30,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/toe-campaign-20261015/exact_extensions/exact_recheck_R3.log","additions":3,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/toe-campaign-20261015/exact_extensions/exact_recheck_R3.py","additions":27,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/toe-campaign-20261015/exact_extensions/fastR3.py","additions":193,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/toe-campaign-20261015/exact_extensions/fastR3_3.log","additions":8,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/toe-campaign-20261015/exact_extensions/r3_triv.out","additions":25,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/toe-campaign-20261015/exact_extensions/r3_triv.sing","additions":130,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/physics-loops/toe-campaign-20261015/exact_extensions/r3_triv_p.sing","additions":130,"deletions":0},{"path":".claude/science/